usbfs is Linux's kernel too.

/dev/bus/usb, its ioctls and the descriptor layouts in <linux/usb/ch9.h>.
UsbDeviceLinux exists to hand out a UsbDeviceHandleUsbfs, so the two belong
on the same side of the line the rest of this series draws.

use_udev is already false in this build, so UsbServiceLinux is not compiled
either and UsbService::Create has no backend to return - which is the truth
about a machine whose USB is xHCI and HID inside its own kernel rather than a
filesystem a browser opens.

